name 'aif_pl_function-intro2-L21_Python'
title 'title'
description 'description here'

markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>Creating and Using Functions in Python</h1>
<p>Now that we know why functions are useful, let's look at how to make one in Python.</p>
<p>There are a few key steps:</p>

<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; max-width: 900px; margin: auto;">

  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 25px;">
    <div style="background: #E4E2F8; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; width: 60px; height: 60px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; flex-shrink:0;">
      <span style="font-size: 22px; font-weight: bold; color: #1F1976;">1</span>
    </div>
    <div style="flex: 1; background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #E4E2F8; border-left: 6px solid #4C42CF; padding: 12px 18px; border-radius: 10px;">
      <h3 style="color: #1F1976; font-weight: bold; margin: 0 0 6px 0;">Give your function a name</h3>
      <p>A function needs a name so you can refer to it later. Pick something that describes what the function does, like <code style="font-size:14px;">greet&#95;user</code> or <code style="font-size:14px;">calculate&#95;total</code>. Remember to use <code style="font-size:14px;">snake&#95;case</code>!</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 25px;">
    <div style="background: #E4E2F8; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; width: 60px; height: 60px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; flex-shrink:0;">
      <span style="font-size: 22px; font-weight: bold; color: #1F1976;">2</span>
    </div>
    <div style="flex: 1; background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #E4E2F8; border-left: 6px solid #4C42CF; padding: 12px 18px; border-radius: 10px;">
      <h3 style="color: #1F1976; font-weight: bold; margin: 0 0 6px 0;">Use the def keyword to define the function</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 14px;">In Python, every function starts with the word <b>def</b> (short for define), followed by the function's name and parentheses <code style="font-size:14px;">()</code> and a colon <code style="font-size:14px;">:</code>.</p>
      <div style="max-width:400px; padding:16px 20px; box-sizing:border-box; overflow-x:auto; white-space:nowrap; background-color:#1C1F2A; color:#FFFFFF; border-radius:10px; font-family:'Courier New',Courier,monospace; font-size:16px; line-height:1.7;">
        <span style="color:#6FCAFF;">def</span> <span style="color:#F07FB0;">greet</span>():
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 25px;">
    <div style="background: #E4E2F8; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; width: 60px; height: 60px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; flex-shrink:0;">
      <span style="font-size: 22px; font-weight: bold; color: #1F1976;">3</span>
    </div>
    <div style="flex: 1; background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #E4E2F8; border-left: 6px solid #4C42CF; padding: 12px 18px; border-radius: 10px;">
      <h3 style="color: #1F1976; font-weight: bold; margin: 0 0 6px 0;">Write the code you want to run (inside the function)</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 14px;">The code inside the function is indented, usually 4 spaces or a tab. This tells Python what belongs to the function.</p>
      <div style="max-width:400px; padding:16px 20px; box-sizing:border-box; overflow-x:auto; white-space:nowrap; background-color:#1C1F2A; color:#FFFFFF; border-radius:10px; font-family:'Courier New',Courier,monospace; font-size:16px; line-height:1.7;">
        <span style="color:#6FCAFF;">def</span> <span style="color:#F07FB0;">greet</span>():<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style="color:#6FCAFF;">print</span>(<span style="color:#F07FB0;">"Hello, World!"</span>)
      </div>
      <div style="background-color: #D5EFFF; color: #06338D; border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px 14px; margin-top: 12px;">
        <p>➡️ <i>Indentation matters in Python! If the lines aren't indented, Python won't know they're part of the function.</i></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 25px;">
    <div style="background: #E4E2F8; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; width: 60px; height: 60px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; flex-shrink:0;">
      <span style="font-size: 22px; font-weight: bold; color: #1F1976;">4</span>
    </div>
    <div style="flex: 1; background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #E4E2F8; border-left: 6px solid #4C42CF; padding: 12px 18px; border-radius: 10px;">
      <h3 style="color: #1F1976; font-weight: bold; margin: 0 0 6px 0;">Call the function to make it run</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 14px;">Just defining a function doesn't run it. You have to call it by typing its name with parentheses:</p>
      <div style="max-width:400px; padding:16px 20px; box-sizing:border-box; overflow-x:auto; white-space:nowrap; background-color:#1C1F2A; color:#FFFFFF; border-radius:10px; font-family:'Courier New',Courier,monospace; font-size:16px; line-height:1.7;">
        <span style="color:#6FCAFF;">def</span> <span style="color:#F07FB0;">greet</span>():<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style="color:#6FCAFF;">print</span>(<span style="color:#F07FB0;">"Hello, World!"</span>)<br>
        <br>
       <span style="color:#F07FB0;">greet</span>()
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<h2>Let's practice!</h2>
MARKDOWN
